Confirmed that dropping the offending keycode 86 definition out of
keymaps/en-us fixes the problem. Scratch build for Fedora Rawhide was
https://koji.fedoraproject.org/koji/taskinfo?taskID=3D23814932 , I'll
probably send this out as an official build so I can get os-autoinst
built without hacking up the tests, but as the files are generated by
qemu-keymap just hand editing the file isn't really the 'right' solution
for upstream; someone will need to tweak qemu-keymap, or else leave the
keymap alone but somehow tweak the relevant bits in qemu/ui/keymaps.c
and fix the problem that way.

-- =

